Package: liblapin-dev
Section: libdevel
Priority: optional
Architecture: any
Depends:
  ${misc:Depends}
Recommends:
  liblapin-build-tools (= ${binary:Version})
Suggests:
  liblapin-utils (= ${binary:Version})
Description: Multimedia/game development library with C bindings (static)
 LibLapin is a multimedia/game development library built on top of SFML,
 providing C bindings, additional game-specific tools, and a configuration
 module that handles most formats and includes an original Turing-complete
 language, Dabsic. It is used by independent game studios and by several
 computing schools to teach C development and multimedia programming.

Package: liblapin-build-tools
Section: devel
Priority: optional
Architecture: any
Depends:
  ${misc:Depends},
  g++,
  liblapin-dev (= ${binary:Version})
Description: compiler helper programs for LibLapin development
 This package contains the bcc and b++ helper programs used to compile and
 link programs against LibLapin. These tools depend on liblapin-dev because
 they require the LibLapin development files to be useful.

Package: liblapin-utils
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: any
Depends:
  ${shlibs:Depends},
  ${misc:Depends}
Suggests:
  liblapin-dev
Description: utility programs shipped with LibLapin
 This package contains the standalone command-line utility programs shipped
 with LibLapin and built from misc/programs/utils like mergeconf.
